    {
      "wanneer": "2026-10-28T17:24:58+00:00",
      "gebeurtenis": "taal_na_skrywer",
      "punte": [
        "fix: [taal] in 'terwyl hulle werk en 'n vaste huis soek': 'terwyl hulle werk en 'n vaste huis soek' can be read as 'while they work' or as 'while they look for work'.",
        "fix: [taal] in 'waar minder mense op elke stuk grond woon as in 'n dorp of stad, in ge': In the definition, 'in gemeenskappe en op plase' trails after the comparison and dangles.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Waarvan mense af trek': Block heading: the separable verb is written apart, and joined as 'aftrek' it means 'deduct'; something like 'Waarvandaan mense wegtrek' would be correct, but a heading may not be applicable by script.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Die trek loop nie een rigting nie': Block heading: 'loop nie net in een rigting nie' is the idiomatic form; left as a flag because it is a heading.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'werk wat beter betaal as die werk by die huis': 'by die huis' here means the home area people come from, but a learner can read 'die werk by die huis' as housework; the same phrase recurs in 'Waarvan mense af trek'. Fixing it means choosing a wording for the home area, which is a content choice."
      ]
    },
